WEBVTT

00:00.900 --> 00:12.650
Four real public tender evaluations. 32 firms. 1,752 pages.

00:18.800 --> 00:23.850
Tender evaluation is slow, inconsistent and hard to defend.

00:24.550 --> 00:35.675
Ranking agreed with the panel in two cases; one inconclusive; one too close.

00:35.975 --> 00:43.250
Code checks found errors the panels left unremarked.

00:43.950 --> 00:52.925
Shown next on a fictional tender, read by a live AI model.

00:53.625 --> 00:57.200
Every step listed, with its status in words.

00:57.500 --> 01:01.550
Every file is registered before anything is read.

01:01.850 --> 01:06.950
The evaluator confirms the criteria before any score is proposed.

01:07.250 --> 01:11.625
A declaration of interests comes before any submission is shown.

01:12.325 --> 01:18.275
On a mandatory gate, the evaluator decides first.

01:18.575 --> 01:23.875
Then Evalia's reading, with its quote checked on the page.

01:24.175 --> 01:29.475
After each decision, Evalia says what it changed.

01:30.175 --> 01:36.100
One requirement, every bidder, side by side.

01:36.400 --> 01:41.400
One in five is drawn at random and decided again, blind.

01:42.100 --> 01:52.400
Code recomputes every price line: this one is $180,000 out.

01:52.700 --> 01:59.500
On a panel, each evaluator works alone, by role.

02:00.200 --> 02:06.075
At closing: the evaluator's own judgement, not an agreement rate.

02:06.375 --> 02:10.125
Every decision and reason recorded, with a statement on the use of AI.

02:10.425 --> 02:14.725
Debrief letters for every bidder, drafted without AI.

02:15.425 --> 02:23.750
No client yet. Next: a pilot on a live procurement.
